        "message": "Here are reliable sentence starters you can memorize and drop in immediately to break a freeze during the exam: **To state your main point directly:**\n* \"The primary cause/factor of [concept from prompt] is...\"\n* \"In this context, [concept] refers to...\" **To explain how or why:**\n* \"This mechanism works by...\"\n* \"Specifically, this occurs because...\" **To bring in an example or detail:**\n* \"A clear example of this is...\"\n* \"This is demonstrated when...\" **To wrap up the answer:**\n* \"Consequently, the main impact is...\"\n* \"Ultimately, this shows that...\" If your mind goes completely blank, write down just the first prompt word and one of these stems. Forcing out that first neutral phrase usually unblocks the rest of the thought. *(If you meant a script to email your professor about the retake instead, let me know and I can give you that.)*",
